  "body": "### What is the issue with the HTML Standard?\n\nBy this I mean specifically that there is no way to tell whether a details element was toggled by a user clicking on its summary element, a user clicking on the summary element of another details element with the same name, or some other reason.\n\nHaving this reason on the \"toggle\" (and elsewhere-mentioned \"beforetoggle\" #9743) events would simplify logic around, for example, tab-like interfaces where one of a set of details elements should always be open.",
